PROPERTY DAMAGE LIABILITY WAIVER℠
All rentals are required to carry and maintain $100,000 of property damage liability coverage. The resident is responsible for
damages caused by the resident or the resident’s guests. The contractual requirement can be satisfied in two different ways:
1. The Property Damage Liability WaiverSM (PDLW®). Through the payment of $12.00 of additional rent each month,
in accordance with the terms of your residential rental agreement, the PDLW® waives your obligation to indemnify
the property owner for damages arising from fire, smoke, explosion, water discharge, or sewer backup caused by your
accidental acts or omissions as further described in your rental agreement up to $100,000 per occurrence. THIS
WAIVER ONLY WAIVES YOUR LIABILITY TO THE PROPERTY OWNER AND DOES NOT WAIVE YOUR
LIABILITY TO ANY THIRD PARTIES. THIS WAIVER ONLY APPLIES TO DAMAGE CAUSED BY YOUR
ACCIDENTAL ACTS OR OMISSIONS AND DOES NOT APPLY TO DAMAGES CAUSED BY YOUR DELIBERATE
OR INTENTIONAL ACTS OR OMISSIONS. THIS WAIVER ONLY APPLIES UP TO $100,000 PER OCCURRENCE;
ANY AMOUNT IN EXCESS OF $100,000 REMAINS SUBJECT TO THE TERMS OF THE RENTAL AGREEMENT.
In situations where the property owner’s covered damages are under $100,000, and subject to the terms of any
applicable owner insurance policy, personal property coverage may be available as an amenity, provided that in no
event shall the sum of the property owner’s covered damages and all amounts paid to affected residents exceed
$100,000. Opt Out
2. A personal renter’s insurance policy (HO4). Initial as indicated below and provide proof of property damage liability
insurance coverage, including a minimum of $100,000 of liability coverage per incident for the perils of fire, smoke,
explosion, water discharge, and sewer backup and listing the property owner as an “Interested Party.” If you fail to
provide proof of the required coverage prior to the commencement of your lease, your rental will be automatically
placed in the Property Damage Liability WaiverSM and you will be charged an additional rent of $12.00 per month. If
the required coverage should be canceled or lapse for any reason, the property owner reserves the right to place your
rental in the Property Damage Liability WaiverSM and charge you an additional rent of $12.00 per month as well as
$200.00 additional rent for the first month.
