the date specified in the notice, or if such remedy cannot be completed within 14 days, but is commenced within the 14-day period and is
pursued in good faith to completion within a reasonable time, the Rental Agreement shall not terminate by reason of the breach.
The Landlord may recover actual damages and obtain injunctive relief in magistrate's or circuit court without posting bond for any
noncompliance by the Tenant with the Rental Agreement or Paragraphs 18 or 19 above. If the Tenant's noncompliance is willful other than
nonpayment of rent, the Landlord may recover reasonable attorney's fees. If the Tenant's nonpayment of rent is not in good faith, the
Landlord is entitled to reasonable attorney's fees.
