IN SCHOOL
EXPOSED: More than 6 million children have asthma, a condition
triggered by tobacco smoke, dust mites, air pollution, pets and mold.7
SICK DAY: Asthma is a leading cause of school absenteeism.8
TEST TAKERS: Children in classrooms with higher outdoor ventilation
rates tend to achieve higher scores on standardized math and reading
tests than those in poorly ventilated classrooms.9
7 www.cdc.gov/asthma/most_recent_data.htm. www.cdc.gov/asthma/faqs.htm
