Johnson Property Management Home Ownership Program
Our hope at Johnson Property Management, LLC (JPM) is that you will be a long-term tenant through our
company, and that we are able to provide you with the highest level of service during your rental term. For
many people, renting is the first step towards eventually purchasing a home of their own, and we would love
the opportunity to help you achieve that goal when it comes time! Through your tenancy in a Johnson
Property Management, LLC rental property, you are immediately building your credit that will help you qualify
for a home loan. Through our home ownership program, you are also able to receive a portion of your
monthly rental payment back to apply towards the purchase of your own home! Please contact Andrew
Johnson for details at 208-884-3310 extension 100, or andrewjohnsonidaho@gmail.com.
The program details are as follows:
 As a JPM tenant, you are automatically enrolled in this program. There are no costs or fees
charged to you for using this program.
 You can earn a maximum credit over the course of your first twelve months of tenancy,
representing the completion of at least your initial one-year rental agreement term. The credit
amount is 10% of your base rent charge! (If your monthly rent charge is $1,000/month x 12
months, your purchase credit would be $1,200)
 Rent is not marked up. The credit you receive is paid to you through the commissions that Andrew
Johnson, owner of JPM and sales agent with Initial Point Real Estate, otherwise would have
received.
 You must have Andrew Johnson, or other approved Initial Point Real Estate agent facilitate the
purchase for you as your exclusive buyers agent.
 We have great relationships with various lenders if you need a referral for a mortgage lender.
 Credit can apply to any real estate purchase of any new or pre-owned home located in Boise,
Nampa, Meridian, Caldwell, or surrounding areas of the Idaho Treasure Valley. Credit will be
applied at the time of closing.
If a tenant moves away from a JPM managed rental property, or if a managed property is removed
from our inventory, credits will not continue and are forfeited. Initial lease terms need to be completed with no
late rent payments or lease violations in order to qualify for the purchase credits.
