TERMS & CONDITIONS
CUSTOMER SERVICE: We commit to being professional and courteous, by
communicating clearly with the customer, and to respect the customer's property
and home. Our painters promise to give their best effort on every job.

--- Page 14 ---

WARRANTY: We warranty our workmanship for two years. Simply call us up and
we'll return to your property promptly to address and correct the issue. Warranty
does not include work involving stain, ␀ooring/patios or rotted wood.
PROJECT OVERVIEW :
-This estimate is based on the condition of the substrates mentioned at the time
of the estimate with regards to amount of prep work needed, cleanliness, etc. Any
deviation from the current conditions quoted out by our estimators will result in a
reassessment of the project and could result in a higher or lower cost.
-Surfaces to be painted include up to 2 coats in order to achieve adequate
coverage unless noted. Stain, one coat unless requested or required and noted. If
additional coats are needed, additional cost will be advised and applied as
needed.
CHANGES TO CONTRACT (change order):
1. If you request a change to be made to the work being done, including the
amount of prep work or changes in products, ␀nishes (sheen), number of colors,
or number of coats, then the price will be adjusted to re␀ect the changes in the
change order.
2. All paints and stains (once tinted) are not returnable, if you decide to change
your mind on a color after the color has been selected and ordered, then you will
be charged for the extra material as well as the extra labor involved (if any) to
achieve your newly requested color/sheen.
3. Any specialty ␀nish, such as a dry erase wall, faux ␀nish, venetian plaster,
lacquer, glitter paint, or anything of this nature outside of the scope of brushing
and rolling two coats of standard paint on a wall ceiling or trim will result in an
extra cost outside of a standard pricing.
REPAIRING DAMAGED WALLS: Please keep in mind that it is near impossible to
match textures exactly. When our painting crews ␀x holes in walls and ceilings
they will give their best effort to repair and retexture over the problem area.
Please be aware that we are not a drywall/texturing company, and do not
specialize in drywall/texture repair. It is possible that a drywall/ texture speci␀c
company could do a better job than us at texturing. If you feel that you'd rather

--- Page 15 ---

have a professional texturing/drywall company ␀x patches please have them do
so prior to our arrival.
HOW COLORS AFFECT YOUR PRICE: The pricing shown in the quote is based on
using up to 2 sheens on the project unless otherwise speci␀ed (walls/trim). For
any additional colors/sheens or accent walls, additional charges will apply. We
charge $75 for each additional color or sheen as well as $125 for each accent
wall. All additional costs pertaining to additional colors/sheen are re␀ective of
extra work/material. Examples; extra tools being cleaned, extra paint, extra tape
and masking supplies, extra time required to break away from the standard way
of painting a room or house.
UNFORESEEN CONDITIONS: We do our best to identify every aspect of the
painting project in the original quote to provide you with an accurate price on the
project. However, there may be some unforeseen conditions out of our control
that occur. These may include: poor lighting, rotten wood that we may not see
until after we pressure wash and start scraping, errors made on the customers
behalf by bumping walls or marring up a freshly painted surface, etc. Additional
work will be charged at $65 per man hour plus material or will be quoted out by
the project manager.
Moving furniture that has not been moved previously by the customer unless
otherwise speci␀ed in the estimate will also be done at a rate of $65 per man
hour.
DELAYS (Does not include weather):
If delays occur that prevent us from completing the work ie colors not chosen, or
other contractors on site, an additional scheduling con␀ict fee of $150 per day
may be incurred. If job is in process and is not allowed to be ␀nished for any
reason, a scheduling con␀ict fee of $150 per day delayed may be incurred as well.
Our goal is to provide you with a top-notch service and we can not be delayed
during our project. Delay fee does not apply to weather.
PRICING: We have quoted you a ␀xed price estimate for your painting project- the
price you see on your quote is the price you will pay. Any variances from the

--- Page 16 ---

original quote in regards to number of colors/sheens, amount of prep work,
additional surfaces, etc. will result in an increased price. All quotes are good for
90 days. After 90 days, a new estimate may need to be conducted and a new
quote issued as prices may change.
PAYMENT TERMS: We request a 30% down payment upon booking the project.
The remaining 70% is due on the day of completion. If the job total is over $7000,
an additional 30% is due after the second day of work is completed. The
remainder will be due after the project has been completed. If for any reason
payment for the completed work is not paid in full within 24 hours of the
completion of the project, then a $50 late penalty will be added for each day that
invoice is past due. A lien may be placed for extreme circumstances.
PAYMENT OPTIONS: Cash, check, all major credit cards. We waive the processing
fee on all deposit payments. There is a 2.9% processing fee added to all ␀nal
payments made via credit card. Checks should be made payable to Hill Country
Painting and will be collected on the ␀nal walk through.
3 DAY RIGHT OF REFUSAL - You, the buyer, may cancel this transaction at any
time prior to midnight of the third business day after the date of this transaction.
The law requires that the contractor give you a notice explaining your right to
cancel. If you choose to cancel this contract after the proscribed 3 day period, the
30% deposit is non-refundable. However, if job is cancelled after 3rd day, the
deposit may be used for a different job of equal or greater value within 12 months
of the payment of the deposit.
