Repair Requests
All repair requests must be submitted in writing per the terms of your lease agreement. Requests must include
your name, daytime and evening telephone numbers, property address and specific problem or request. You
may submit your request by going online to http://www.gdaapm.com/maintenance. You will be contacted within 72
hours to schedule an appointment with one of our vendors. If it is determined the repair is due to tenant abuse
or neglect, Tenant will be responsible for the cost of the repair. If the Vendor finds no issues upon arrival
the Tenant will be responsible for the cost of the trip fee charged by the Vendor. If you fail to meet a contractor
once you have agreed to an appointment time, you will be charged a $75 trip fee.
If you break or reschedule two appointments. we will release a key to the vendor to access your home and
take care of the repair.
Emergency Repairs
Please report anything relating to the property under the lease that is threatening to life, health, or the property.
Property Meld is not monitored after hours.
Call (512) 439-3602 for afterhours emergencies to speak to a member of our team.
Climate Control: No air conditioning if temperature is over 90 degrees or no heat if temperature is forecast
to be below freezing.
Broken pipe or free flowing water: Turn off water valve or exterior water main.
