A 12. Renter Contents Liability Loss means the Actual Cash Value or Replacement Cost due to burglary
or destruction of Renter Contents due to a Peril located within the Covered Property.
a
b 13. Renter Premises Legal Liability Loss means:
1 a) settlements or judgments fully or partially resolving the Renter’s liability for
Property Damage resulting from a Peril; and
c b) the cost of a lawyer, selected by the Property Manager, to defend the Renter
from liability for Property Damage resulting from a Peril.
d 14. Replacement Cost means the cost to repair or replace Renter Contents, at the time of loss or
damage, whether that property has sustained partial or total loss or damage, with material of like kind and
quality, without a deduction for deterioration, depreciation and obsolescence.
e
f 15. Security Deposit means the amount indicated as the Security Deposit on the Lease Addendum or
the Lease Agreement.
g
h 16. Deductible. We will pay for any covered loss to covered property only when it exceeds the
applicable deductible shown on the lease addendum.
Provided, the Property Manager shall not have any further obligation to settle or defend the Renter once the
