a) Fire or lightning;
b) smoke, but not smoke caused by agricultural smudging or industrial
operations;
c) explosion;
d) accidental discharge or overflow of water or steam;
e) sprinkler leakage;
f) falling objects, but only if the roof or exterior wall of the Covered Property
is damaged by the falling object, and damage to the falling object itself is not
covered;
g) freezing of plumbing, heating or air conditioning;
h) discharge or overflow from appliances;
i) weight of Renter’s personal property, but not for purposes of a Renter
Contents Liability Loss;
j) burglary, but only if a police report was promptly filed by the Renter, and this
does not include mysterious disappearance, or lost or misplaced property;
Burglary means the unlawful taking of property within premises that has
been closed and in which there are visible marks evidencing forcible entry.
Proof of purchase and receipts are required.
